---
pagination:
  data: legacyRedirects.pages
  size: 1
  alias: r
permalink: "{{ r.from }}index.html"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#-
  Forwarding pages for the addresses of the old msca09aa.org WordPress site
  (data/redirects.csv, plus the old_url of every archived Delegate's Corner post).
  GitHub Pages cannot send real redirects, so each old address gets this tiny page:
  it forwards at once (instant meta refresh = permanent redirect for search engines, plus canonical,
  plus script). No noindex: it would contradict the redirect and stop the old address's links from
  counting for the new page; a forwarding page is never indexed itself, and it stays out of the
  sitemap (eleventyExcludeFromCollections) and the site search (data-pagefind-ignore).
  The canonical leaves out a #section (search engines ignore it); the refresh, script and link keep it.
  A row whose new page is Spanish (/es/…, e.g. the Spanish flyer's /es/prf2028/) gets a Spanish page.
  Path prefix (a site in a sub-folder, https://<user>.github.io/<repo>/): HtmlBasePlugin adds it to
  the visible links AND to the meta refresh address, so both are written here without it. The
  script is not rewritten by the plugin, so its address (target) includes site.base itself.
  Either way the forwarding works whether or not the old address was typed with its final "/".
  Addresses ending in * in the CSV, and old addresses inside folders of this site, are forwarded by the
  "page not found" page instead (/assets/js/redirects.js) — except the old address of a renamed calendar event
  (/events/<slug>/ or /es/events/<slug>/), which gets a page here (EVENT_PAGE in eleventy.config.js).
-#}
{%- set en = { code: "en" } -%}
{%- set es = { code: "es" } -%}
{#- the page's language: that of the new page (L1). An English row also links the Spanish copy below. -#}
{%- set L1 = es if r.to.startsWith("/es/") else en -%}
{%- set target = site.base + r.to.slice(1) -%}
{#- Page titles are stored already escaped ("District 1 &amp; 3"): strip turns them back into plain
    text, so the output below escapes them exactly once. titleEs is empty for a Spanish row (/es/es/… is no page). -#}
{%- set toTitle = r.to | titleForUrl(collections.all) | strip -%}
{%- set titleEs = ("/es" + r.to) | titleForUrl(collections.all) | strip -%}
{#- a short address of this site (data/redirects.csv note "Short address …", e.g. /report/) has not moved anywhere:
    its page just says it is taking you there; a renamed event (/events/… or /es/events/…) has only a new address -#}
{%- set renamed = r.from.startsWith("/events/") or r.from.startsWith("/es/events/") -%}
{%- set movedKey = "legacy.short" if r.note.startsWith("Short address") else ("legacy.renamed" if renamed else "legacy.moved") -%}
{%- set moved = movedKey | tIf(L1) -%}
{%- set movedEs = movedKey | tIf(es) -%}
{#- Link previews: chat apps (WhatsApp, Slack, X …) build their card from this page itself and do not follow the
    refresh, so it carries the new page's card (pageForUrl in eleventy.config.js): its title, description and picture,
    or the site's description and picture in the page's language when it has none. -#}
{%- set tgt = r.to | pageForUrl(collections.all) -%}
{%- set canonical = r.to.split('#')[0] | absUrl(site.url + '/') -%}
{%- set desc = (tgt.description or ("site.description" | t(L1))) | strip -%}
{%- set ogAlt = (tgt.ogImageAlt if tgt.ogImage else ("site.og_image_alt" | t(L1))) | strip -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ L1.code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ toTitle or r.to }} · {{ "site.title_suffix" | t(L1) }}</title>
  <meta name="msca-legacy-redirect" content="{{ r.to }}">
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ r.to }}">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical }}">
  <meta name="description" content="{{ desc | truncate(300) }}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ 'site.name' | t(L1) }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ (tgt.title | strip) or toTitle or r.to }}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ desc | truncate(200) }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical }}">
  <meta property="og:locale" content="{{ 'es_US' if L1.code == 'es' else 'en_US' }}">
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ (tgt.ogImage or ('/assets/img/social-card-es.jpg' if L1.code == 'es' else '/assets/img/social-card.jpg')) | absUrl(site.url + '/') }}">
  {%- if not tgt.ogImage %}
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
  <meta property="og:image:type" content="image/jpeg">
  {%- else %}
  {%- if tgt.ogImageWidth and tgt.ogImageHeight %}
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="{{ tgt.ogImageWidth }}">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ tgt.ogImageHeight }}">
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if tgt.ogImageType %}
  <meta property="og:image:type" content="{{ tgt.ogImageType }}">
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if ogAlt %}
  <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ ogAlt }}">
  {%- endif %}
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  {%- if ogAlt %}
  <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="{{ ogAlt }}">
  {%- endif %}
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light; }
    body { margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: grid; place-items: center; font: 17px/1.5 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; color: #1c2033;
      background: radial-gradient(40rem 24rem at 0% 0%, #d6eefa, transparent 60%), radial-gradient(40rem 24rem at 100% 100%, #e6e1f5, transparent 60%), #f5f6fb; }
    main { box-sizing: border-box; width: min(34rem, calc(100% - 2rem)); margin: 1rem; padding: 1.75rem; border-radius: 1.5rem; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 12px 40px -16px rgb(19 23 43 / .25); }
    .site { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #5b6078; }
    .old { margin: 0; font: 600 .9rem/1.4 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; color: #676c84; text-decoration: line-through; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .arrow { display: block; margin: .35rem 0; font-size: 1.4rem; color: #d63b31; }
    a { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; min-height: 44px; color: #1f6fa8; font-weight: 700; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #1f6fa8; outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: .25rem; }
    .es { font-weight: 600; font-size: .95rem; }
    p.note { margin: .25rem 0 .75rem; color: #3d4259; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main data-pagefind-ignore="all">
    <p class="site">{{ "site.name" | t(L1) }}</p>
    <p class="old">{{ r.from }}</p>
    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
    {%- if moved %}<p class="note">{{ moved }}</p>{% endif %}
    <a href="{{ r.to }}">{{ toTitle or r.to }} →</a>
    {%- if titleEs %}
    {%- if movedEs %}<p class="note" lang="es">{{ movedEs }}</p>{% endif %}
    <a class="es" href="{{ '/es' + r.to }}" lang="es" hreflang="es">{{ titleEs }} →</a>
    {%- endif %}
  </main>
  <script>location.replace({{ target | dump | safe }});</script>
</body>
</html>
